{"id": "EUVD-2026-103590", "enisaUuid": "8ef64285-2137-3332-93a7-b56315a7c2da", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nata: libata-scsi: bound the ATA passthru sense descriptor writes\n\nWhen an ATA PASS-THROUGH command to an ATAPI device fails, the sense\nbuffer holds the device's REQUEST SENSE reply, and\nata_scsi_set_passthru_sense_fields() trusts its additional length\nbyte, sb[7], when adding the ATA Status Return descriptor.  A faulty\nor malicious device can use that to make the kernel read and write\npast the 96-byte buffer in three ways:\n\n- scsi_sense_desc_find() is passed sb[7] + 8 as the buffer length, so\n  its clamp against sb[7] does nothing and the walk runs off the end.\n- A type-9 descriptor found near the end is filled in unchecked.\n- A new descriptor at sb[8 + len] needs len + 22 bytes, not len + 14,\n  so len 75..82 writes up to 8 bytes past the end.\n\nReproduced with KASAN under qemu, with the emulated ATAPI REQUEST SENSE\nreply patched:\n\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds in scsi_sense_desc_find+0x1a5/0x210\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds in ata_scsi_qc_complete+0x1a15/0x1a50\n\nBoth are gone with this patch, and a valid descriptor is still filled\nin.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:18:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:28", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c698f6deabf680f8f4a1727ef2dc80fe78815fbf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d9a7147b93624660626cd7c3b1143715699e1f5c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1603abb0c50420e97cf4a1feddbd5e183c5fdf86", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/80fbb0bc4d11683c88f2f9d3997ea02fcada5408", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/80320b278fea07ffcda3f57b67b61658e0a4e1ca"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gq8r-6748-x6m5", "CVE-2026-98545"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0dececb3-892c-3ff5-a407-145b43f0f206", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "16b3fa1d-bdac-3743-a361-2efc5e8e9474", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10.3 <6.11"}, {"id": "35f4679c-5feb-3492-97a3-6aa19f7af696", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "97981926224afe17ba3e22e0c2b7dd8b516ee574 <1603abb0c50420e97cf4a1feddbd5e183c5fdf86"}, {"id": "3891edcb-7bf5-37a2-ad12-50c52252ca7b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.44 <6.6.158"}, {"id": "41a5e5a8-5339-3e46-8a3c-846d46d6e25e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "67d9d0b6ae4aaf2c4cef103a96a145c7fdfb15f8"}, {"id": "4e50b245-ef81-3b80-9700-959d4646abfc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "97981926224afe17ba3e22e0c2b7dd8b516ee574 <80fbb0bc4d11683c88f2f9d3997ea02fcada5408"}, {"id": "6bad346a-ee54-3d48-bda2-8d9248198176", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "76d8efd0-263b-3ee0-a15b-40985975069f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "95ffcc4d-b290-39b7-b870-51dc60f6d4fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "99866ddb-0954-3d04-9ab4-31a1f2487b38", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "97981926224afe17ba3e22e0c2b7dd8b516ee574 <80320b278fea07ffcda3f57b67b61658e0a4e1ca"}, {"id": "a7a1e647-b4d5-3651-862e-0c27b168c216", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "97981926224afe17ba3e22e0c2b7dd8b516ee574 <d9a7147b93624660626cd7c3b1143715699e1f5c"}, {"id": "b6eb4291-778f-3c4e-9827-86e5ff7e5b14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "c91f3b3e-e370-3ffc-8f1b-bd9b745dd348", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ce477199c53e3db5a09